section: compiler
synopsis: Accumulating coverage data over multiple runs is no longer the default
issues: #27956
mrs: !16826
description:
  Programs compiled using :ghc-flag:`-fhpc` will, when executed, no longer read
  an existing ``.tix`` file for the program and add coverage data to it by
  default. Instead, the new default is to overwrite an existing ``.tix`` file
  with only the coverage data from the latest run.

  :rts-flag:`--read-tix-file=\<yes|no\>` can be used to control this behaviour
  as before. This release merely changes the default from
  ``--read-tix-file=yes`` to ``--read-tix-file=no``.

  Additionally, the deprecation warning introduced in GHC 9.12 to warn about
  this change of default behaviour in the future has been removed.
